  "narration": {
    "pattern_romaji": "A wa B ja nai desu",
    "pattern_jp": "AはBじゃないです",
    "pattern_english": "A is not B",
    "slots": [
      {
        "slot": "A",
        "fits": "the topic: a person (私, a name like けん), a thing (これ), or a time or place (あした, きょう)"
      },
      {
        "slot": "B",
        "fits": "a noun that A is NOT: a job (学生, かいしゃいん, せんせい), a nationality (日本人), a thing (コーヒー), or the weather (雨)"
      }
    ],
    "segments": [
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Welcome back! Today's pattern is {AはBじゃないです}. It means: A is not B."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "AはBじゃないです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "That's A is not B. You already know {AはBです}, which means A is B. Today we just make it negative."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Here are the slots. A is the topic: a person, a thing, whatever you're talking about. The little word {は} comes right after it and marks it as the topic."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "B is a noun, like a job, a nationality, or a drink. Then, where you used to say {です}, you now say {じゃないです}. That ending means is not."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Notice the word order. In English, the word not comes in the middle: I am not a student. In Japanese, the not comes at the very end, glued to the ending. You don't know it's negative until the last moment, so listen to the end of the sentence!"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Let's build one. Start with I."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "私"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Add the topic marker."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "私は"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "As for me. Now add the noun {学生}, student."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "私は学生"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "And finish with the negative ending."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "私は学生じゃないです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "I'm not a student. That's exactly what Ken says in today's dialogue."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Another one. Start with {これ}, this."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "これは"
